-- UNCONSTRAINED binding sharing the surface name `pick` with cmod's. Its dict arity is 0,
-- independently of cmod's 1 (DICT-SEMANTICS §8 I1).
--
-- POLYMORPHIC on purpose, and it is the whole point of this fixture: `s8-i1`'s sibling
-- shape is monomorphic (`Int -> Int`), so a phantom leading dict parameter there is
-- silently consistent -- the define and the call site agree on the extra slot and the
-- printed number comes out right by accident. Here the binding is `a -> a`, so a phantom
-- dict slot makes `pick` RETURN THE DICTIONARY instead of its argument, which is
-- value-observable.
--
-- `use` calls `pick` LOCALLY, inside the module that declares it. That matters: an
-- explicitly IMPORTED occurrence is resolved through `currentImportDefinersRef` and the
-- module-qualified arity tables, which were already source-exact; a LOCAL occurrence takes
-- the bare-name table, which is where a foreign module's same-named constrained binding
-- was able to size this one.
export pick : a -> a
pick x = x

export use : Int -> Int
use n = pick n + 200
